tony k: Hi, how you doing?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Good, how are you?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.000
tony k: Good, let me put my AirPods on here.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Perfect. And I'll just share my screen.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.000
tony k: Okay.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
tony k: One second here, and we'll get ready.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Gotta get ready.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
tony k: I know, I know, it's been crazy this whole week.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no, I can imagine, especially with all the book tours.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.000
tony k: Oh, man, did you, uh, did you talk to Whitney? Because I had a meeting with her and took a bunch of notes.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Oh, really? No, I didn't talk too much to her about your guys' business, yeah.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
tony k: With her.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.000
tony k: Okay.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
tony k: Okay, cool.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Carmen Cruickshank: All right. And then you're in the Indiana area?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
tony k: We're in Indiana. We're about an hour north of Indianapolis.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Oh, okay, that's cool. That's cool.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
tony k: And I've got Carmen with Wedding Industry Ads written down, Google Ads expert. So I'm getting ready to take notes here.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Perfect, perfect. And, um, yeah, normally I'm an hour away from DC, but right now I'm in Maine, so just kind of, like, all over the place. But, uh, yeah, I'm excited to get into it, so let's see.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.000
tony k: Alright.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.000
tony k: Okay.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
tony k: Cool.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Safari…

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.000
tony k: So I will ask a bunch of questions, because, uh…

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Hmm, I see.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.000
tony k: Um, I'm not… I'm not a Google Ads expert like you, so…

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, of course. I love that. Okay, so I did get to check out your account, I think, like, for 10, 15 minutes just to get an idea.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.000
tony k: Mm-hmm.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, but yeah. Okay, so first impression, normally, what I check…

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Carmen Cruickshank: When I see an account, I'm just going to do July. I don't know how long you guys have been running the ads. I think you said since June.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.000
tony k: Uh, actually, actually, I think she started that in…

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:58.000
tony k: either end of March or 1st of April is when we hired the company and pay her to manage the ad. She asked me a few questions of what I was trying to do, and what kind of clientele we're trying to get.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:08.000
tony k: And what I don't want, as far as, like, cheap, uh, cheap wedding venues or DIY wedding venues, they'll search, uh, those keywords.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:18.000
tony k: And just some of the surrounding counties and surrounding cities that we want that are higher income areas.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:25.000
tony k: And those are the ones that we kind of want to, uh… be showing… popping up on. And I go in every day, and I search…

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:38.000
tony k: um… I searched, uh, some of the keywords that I think people would normally search, and just see if I pop up. I don't click on them, so I don't pay, I just want to see if I pop up. I don't think you pay, and correct me if I'm wrong, the impressions are…

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.000
tony k: Not charged if you show up in the search, it's only charged when they click on it, correct?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes, exactly. Yes, that's smart. It's good you know that. Most people don't know that, so… And then, you wanted to get on this ads call because… is it because you're not getting enough, like, contact forms or tours?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.000
tony k: Okay, alright, alright.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
tony k: Okay, alright.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
tony k: So…

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:04.000
tony k: No, she asked… so there's a couple reasons. So, Whitney asked that, too, because when we went… when we started… so I started doing this myself for a little while, and uh…

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:19.000
tony k: I think for a couple months, and then you start getting a lot of phone calls from overseas contractors through Google, and they say, hey, we want to get on this Google call with you, and they work for Google, but their number one.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And…

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:34.000
tony k: Their number one goal is to have a wide search keyword so that your funds just go right away and you keep adding funds. And that's and I realized that after.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.000
tony k: Two weeks, because they had tons of keywords that…

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Right.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:53.000
tony k: I mean, it's just it's worthless. I mean, obviously, I'm going to show up, but I'm only going to be active for 30 minutes of the day. And then I'm I'm I've reached my daily allotted amount that I want to spend. And I'm not going to show up when people get home at night or when they're searching around lunchtime.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.000
tony k: So…

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:00.000
tony k: Um, I went to a convention, and then we met, um…

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:17.000
tony k: Uh, her, uh, Elizabeth, and she says she does that stuff a lot, and it's successful, and she got on there, and obviously, she knows a whole lot more than I do, just like you know a whole lot more than I do, and uh, when she went on there, we started getting really good qualified leads through Google, and these people.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:28.000
tony k: had the funds to spend, and they weren't trying to do DIY, um, and they were intentionally searching for what we have, which is a chapel.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:43.000
tony k: they're searching for wedding venues, and a lot of barns come up, and then they try to alleviate the barn thing, and we just want to hone in on what we have, which is a luxury venue with a wedding chapel, but we also want to show up in the.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.000
tony k: Wedding Barn.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:59.000
tony k: searches, because those people that are searching, and they see a barn, when they see our chapel, half of them said, I didn't know there was a chapel around, so that's why I contacted you guys. So, they don't know what they want until they see it.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Hmm.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:11.000
tony k: That's how we all… that's how we all are. And uh… when they see that, because they see 25 barns, and they see 2 chapels, that's when their eyes open up. So we still wanted to, obviously, get those people.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:15.000
tony k: And so yes, I told her that and she did her thing and.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:28.000
tony k: obviously a lot better than what I was doing, so we started seeing great qualified… I mean, they went to our website. I did a thank you page on our website when I was doing my own, and I… it's through HoneyBook, our CRM.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:48.000
tony k: and when you hit the send button on our, uh, thank you page, I made a… I'm sorry, when you hit the send button on the contact us page, I made a pop-up where it's a separate thank you page, and I took that URL and put it in Google so that I can get a conversion, but I haven't seen that happen, so I don't know where they're going, and then I have a pop-up for, uh.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:06:04.000
tony k: book a tour, if you've been on our website, when you click on that, it goes to Calendly, but there's no pixel, or whatever you call it, to show me the conversion, but she's telling me we're getting a lot of conversions. I'm seeing people fill out on Calendly, Google is where they heard about it, so…

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: You got it.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:17.000
tony k: Um, and then I asked them when I talked to them at the tour, I said, hey, how did you guys hear about us? They said, hey, we went to a search on Google, and uh, and then we saw this barn, or we saw the chapel, and that's how we, you know, went to your website.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm. Okay, that makes sense. Uh…

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:26.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So you want to make sure that everything is proper with conversion tracking, so that… I almost want to look now… so if you go to…

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:34.000
tony k: That, and then also, I don't… I'm not super confident that… because I never heard… hear from our account rep, uh, that I hired.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:40.000
tony k: And, uh, which could be a good and bad thing, but, um, when I talked to Whitney, she said that you guys would give.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
tony k: Um, if I were to do the…

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:58.000
tony k: The accelerator thing with you guys for three months, I'd have the access to the vault. I also get ads like a VIP day with you. You go through Google research or keyword research, then you present a campaign before you launch it.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:13.000
tony k: Once a week office hour with Carmen, the Google ad experts. I wrote those things down that she said that. And all I want to do is I just want to tailor it because if there was such a thing as just set it and forget it, that would be great. Then I would just set it and forget it. But.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Bye. Yeah.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:22.000
tony k: But, you know, I know that's not how it works, and I know that you just kinda… there's no cruise control on the ads market, so you kinda have to tweak.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:28.000
tony k: every now and then, just to make sure your metrics are right. And I log in every day, and I look at the, uh, um…

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:44.000
tony k: I look at my Google Ads account and just to see what the impressions are from the last from yesterday and what the clicks were to the ads and just kind of keep a track of like search keywords that are popular shows up on the app and.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:08:01.000
tony k: And I checked the analytics page just to see kind of how many people we had on our website, which that's not directly correlated just to the Google ads, because when we do TikTok or Instagram, those people organically come from there, not through Google. So.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:12.000
tony k: I'm just trying to get a good feel for when we have a week like this, when it's going up, then you try to hone in on what you were doing that week and tweak that a little bit, so…

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Everything.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:30.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm. No, that's awesome, and, like, I can definitely tell by, like, how you see the Google Ads, like, you'll definitely get it at some point, it's just kind of figuring out the puzzle, because most people I meet that come in the Accelerator, they're just… they see it as set it and forget it, and as much as I want to say testimonials of, like… like, I have a venue in New York City.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.000
tony k: Yes.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:43.000
Carmen Cruickshank: just doing Google Ads, they did $500 a month, which is less than what you guys are spending, and they made, like, $40K in 40 days just from the ads. But that's only because she showed up every week. That's because she was actually, like, putting the time in and effort in.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.000
tony k: Oh, no, I want to do that. I want to… because she was talking about…

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Carmen Cruickshank: 100%.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.000
tony k: She was talking about, you guys do what…

00:08:49.000 --> 00:09:06.000
tony k: Uh, Snowmad does a monthly, uh, Google ad thing where you guys, uh, full service it. And then you have this 3-month accelerator, and then after 3 months, I can still keep you guys and pay a… pay a fee where I can still be with you guys and have access to the…

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:12.000
tony k: Vault and still access with you, just to kind of make sure I'm doing things right, or whatever. It's my understanding, so…

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:28.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no, 100%. And honestly, like, I don't really have a preference for either full service or accelerator. I think I actually prefer meeting with the accelerator people, whether it's like four times a month, two times a month, even one time, because then it's like, I see how it is on their end and then they can check how it is versus like.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.000
tony k: Okay.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.000
tony k: Mm-hmm.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.000
tony k: Right.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:40.000
Carmen Cruickshank: sometimes full-service clients, they also see it as set it and forget it, and I get to see them once a year, and then they're like, oh, what's going on? It's like, I don't get to talk to you and see what's going on, you know what I mean? So, uh… but yeah.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.000
tony k: Yeah, yeah.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So I go to segments sometimes just to see.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:10:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: what conversions we're seeing, because, of course, Google can take things very literally. So if we tell them like we want page views, they just see page views, and they're like, Oh, this account is successful. So right now I don't see any conversions, and I'm kind of curious. So I'm going to go into settings. I don't want to go too fast, too. So I'm going to be.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.000
tony k: Right.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:07.000
tony k: Yeah, oh yeah, this is all new to me, so that's why I hired her originally, because when you go into Google Ads, I mean, there's so many.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:22.000
tony k: puzzle, like what you're doing right now, I didn't know it was available, so… uh, but I want… but I want to learn, because I… I'd like to get a… a good grasp of this, so that when I'm adjusting it, so when… you know, if we… if we got a certain budget we're spending, and then come…

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: It knows the thing.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:38.000
tony k: Uh, engagement season, which usually starts a week before Thanksgiving, all the way through, um, uh, Feb… yeah, to Valentine's Day, because people are proposing, or Thanksgiving, New Year's, Christmas, and Valentine's Day. I want to increase the budget, so I show up more.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Everywhere you're, you know.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:55.000
tony k: and show up on certain keywords, like engagement rings, or whatever, proposals, and… and so I'm tailored into those people that are… because I realize Google has a lot of information on people that are searching, and they would show our ads to them if we're using the correct.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.000
tony k: keywords, so that's what I would like.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no, absolutely. And you definitely, it is a timing thing, because I do notice there's just like an absolute surge with clients in this time, or not this time, but in that time. Okay, so I'll go to settings in campaigns just to see what Google sees the campaign goal is.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.000
tony k: Yep.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.000
tony k: Oh, yeah.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Because if there is no CAM, so right now I see conversion goals is account default. So basically what that means for account default is whatever is just in the account. So right now Google sees submit lead forms, which is the thank you page thing you made. So that is something it is optimizing for, but then also phone calls.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.000
tony k: Okay.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I assume you don't want phone calls, that's mostly what people are. Do you want phone calls or no?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.000
tony k: Oh.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:50.000
tony k: I don't care. I mean, however they want to get a hold of me, but we get phone calls, and people actually are calling… thinking about calling other venues, and they call us.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:12:06.000
tony k: Because they're driving and they're pulling up whatever venue they want. And we pop up first and they say, Hey, is this the elite or is this the Bel Air? And they're all here in town. And I say, No, this is the promise of 2912 and say, Oh, we called, we searched for the elite.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.000
tony k: And then I did that one time, and we just popped up first.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmm.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:27.000
tony k: And then Elite was under, and then they just, you know, they're driving, they click on the first one, and it'll call us, but they were actually searching for the… which is good and bad, because I haven't got anybody booked because of that, because they accidentally picked us, but, um, I also don't want to pay for that if…

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:32.000
tony k: you know, they're trying to get ahold of somebody else here in town, and they… I don't want that conversion to be…

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
tony k: Paid for, so…

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm. No, that makes sense. Yeah, I can definitely see.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:52.000
tony k: But… but I don't… I don't mind. I mean, however way they want to get a hold of me. Ultimately, though, I would like to just show up in the searches for people that are searching for specific… and uh… a barn, but a luxury barn, not a DIY, because once they see the chapel, that's like a trademark for us. Everybody wants to get married there because of that, so…

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Thank you.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Hmm.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:13:04.000
Carmen Cruickshank: No, that makes sense. Yeah, we can definitely keep the phone call leads or we can take it out. So what I do is I just, I'm not going to make this change right now, but I'll go to campaign specific instead.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.000
tony k: Okay.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:22.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And then I'll just choose the campaign goal. And then I'll normally just click the submit lead forms. Because if Google sees all these other things, then let's say we get people clicking how to get directions to your place. If we get like a hundred of those, Google's like, oh, we're doing our job. They're getting these conversions, right? And then it's gone, right?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.000
tony k: Okay.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.000
tony k: Mmhm.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.000
tony k: Okay. Yeah.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So…

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.000
tony k: Right.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:29.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Do you want me to just make it submit lead forms right now, or do you want me to keep it at the phone call and submit lead.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:32.000
tony k: What do you suggest, based on what I've said?

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.000
